## Validation and limits

Use Python 3.11+ and REUSE 5.1.1 for the validation baseline:

    python3 -m pip install reuse==5.1.1
    python3 -m reuse lint
    python3 -m tools.weave_workflow docs-audit

REUSE configuration parses, but full compliance is intentionally incomplete:
the four PDFs in FU-01 still need complete copyright/licensing annotations.
No fictitious licence or copyright holder has been assigned to their fonts.
Validation performed for this change with REUSE 5.1.1:

- REUSE lint exits 1 only for the four PDFs above; 383 of 387 covered files have
  both notices, with zero bad/missing/unused licence texts and zero read errors.
- TOML parsing and annotation-path checks pass: all 385 exact paths exist and
  occur once (two zero-byte Python files are not covered files in REUSE).
- Both sets of 39 pinned prototype SHA-256 records verify unchanged.
- Repository-scope documentation audit passes; git diff --check passes.

The review inspected every tracked filename, repository notices and provenance,
the identified upstream Furo files and PDF font inventories. It is not an
exhaustive upstream source-similarity audit, and no release site/PDF was rebuilt.

REUSE format reference: https://reuse.software/spec/
